Description: Get the loading screen on screen before running queued main thread work
 on_idle() drained the main thread dispatcher before repainting, so the
 preset bundle load queued at start up blocked the main thread for over a
 second before the canvas ever presented. The loading screen was rendered
 the whole time but never reached the screen, leaving the window empty.
 X11 masked this with the splash screen; Wayland does not, since the splash
 is an ordinary toplevel placed by the compositor. Presents a frame first,
 with a 500 ms deadline so start up cannot be postponed indefinitely.
